  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIn [\"upgrade an element\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#concept-upgrade-an-element), step 9 adds the registry to the agent's map:\n\n> [Set](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-set) the [surrounding agent](https://tc39.es/ecma262/#surrounding-agent)'s [active custom element constructor map](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#active-custom-element-constructor-map)[C] to registry.\n\nBut in \"Then, perform the following...\", step 1 tries to remove it from the global object's map:\n\n> [Remove](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-remove) registry's [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global)'s [active custom element constructor map](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#active-custom-element-constructor-map)[C].\n\nThe relevant global object doesn't have a constructor map, so I assume it should be removed from the agent's one instead.\n\n@annevk ",
